
var SUB_FULL={"Path of the Berserker|Frenzy": "When you use Reckless Attack while your Rage is active, the first target you hit on that turn with an attack that uses Strength takes extra damage. Find that extra damage by rolling as many d6s as your Rage Damage bonus and totaling them. This damage is the same type as the weapon or Unarmed Strike you attacked with.", "Path of the Berserker|Mindless Rage": "While your Rage is active, you have Immunity to both the Charmed and Frightened conditions. If either condition is already on you when you enter your Rage, that condition ends.", "Path of the Berserker|Retaliation": "When a creature within 5 feet of you deals damage to you, you can use your Reaction to make a single melee attack against it, using a weapon or an Unarmed Strike.", "Path of the Berserker|Intimidating Presence": "As a Bonus Action, you can terrify others with your menacing presence and primal power. Choose any creatures you like in a 30-foot Emanation from you. Each of them must make a Wisdom saving throw (DC 8 + your Strength modifier + your Proficiency Bonus). A creature that fails gains the Frightened condition, which lasts 1 minute. As each of its turns ends, the Frightened creature repeats the save, and the effect on it ends when it succeeds. You can use this feature once per Long Rest. Spending one use of your Rage (no action required) also restores your use of it.", "Path of the Wild Heart|Animal Speaker": "You can cast Beast Sense and Speak with Animals, but only as Rituals. Your spellcasting ability for them is Wisdom.", "Path of the Wild Heart|Rage of the Wilds": "Your Rage draws on the primal power of animals. Each time you activate your Rage, choose one of the following options to gain. **Bear.** For as long as your Rage lasts, you have Resistance to all damage types other than Force, Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant. **Eagle.** The Bonus Action that activates your Rage can also include the Disengage and Dash actions. For as long as your Rage lasts, a single Bonus Action lets you take both of those actions. **Wolf.** For as long as your Rage lasts, your allies make attack rolls with Advantage against any enemy of yours that is within 5 feet of you.", "Path of the Wild Heart|Aspect of the Wilds": "Choose one of the following options to gain. Each time you finish a Long Rest, you can switch your choice. **Owl.** You gain Darkvision with a range of 60 feet, or, if you have it already, its range grows by 60 feet. **Panther.** You gain a Climb Speed that equals your Speed. **Salmon.** You gain a Swim Speed that equals your Speed.", "Path of the Wild Heart|Nature Speaker": "You can cast Commune with Nature, but only as a Ritual. Your spellcasting ability for it is Wisdom.", "Path of the Wild Heart|Power of the Wilds": "Each time you activate your Rage, choose one of the following options to gain. **Falcon.** For as long as your Rage lasts, you have a Fly Speed equal to your Speed, provided you aren't wearing any armor. **Lion.** For as long as your Rage lasts, each of your enemies within 5 feet of you has Disadvantage on attack rolls that target anyone other than you or another Barbarian with this option active. **Ram.** For as long as your Rage lasts, a melee attack of yours that hits a Large or smaller creature can give that creature the Prone condition.", "Path of the World Tree|Vitality of the Tree": "Your Rage draws on the life force of the World Tree, granting you these benefits. **Vitality Surge.** Each time you activate your Rage, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Barbarian level. **Life-Giving Force.** When each of your turns begins while your Rage is active, you can pick another creature within 10 feet of you to receive Temporary Hit Points. That creature gains Temporary Hit Points equal to the total you get by rolling as many d6s as your Rage Damage bonus. Any of these Temporary Hit Points still left when your Rage ends disappear.", "Path of the World Tree|Branches of the Tree": "While your Rage is active, whenever a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see starts its turn, you can take a Reaction to make spectral branches of the World Tree appear around that creature. It makes a Strength saving throw (DC 8 + your Strength modifier + your Proficiency Bonus). On a failure, it is teleported to an unoccupied space within 5 feet of you that you can see, or else to the nearest unoccupied space you can see. Once the target has teleported, you can lower its Speed to 0 until the current turn ends.", "Path of the World Tree|Battering Roots": "Tendrils of the World Tree reach out from you, so during your turn any Melee weapon with the Heavy or Versatile property has 10 feet of extra reach for you. When one of those weapons hits during your turn, you can use the Push or Topple mastery property as well as a different mastery property that you are using with that weapon.", "Path of the World Tree|Travel Along the Tree": "You can teleport yourself up to 60 feet, arriving in an unoccupied space you can see. You can do this when you activate your Rage, and you can also do it by taking a Bonus Action while your Rage is active. Once per Rage, you can extend the range of that teleport to 150 feet. If you do, you can also take along up to six willing creatures that are within 10 feet of you. Each of them teleports to an unoccupied space you choose within 10 feet of the space where you arrive.", "Path of the Zealot|Divine Fury": "Divine power flows into your strikes. During your Rage, on each of your turns, the first creature that a weapon or Unarmed Strike of yours hits takes extra damage equal to 1d6 + half your Barbarian level (rounded down). The extra damage is Necrotic or Radiant, and you pick the type each time you deal it.", "Path of the Zealot|Warrior of the Gods": "A divine entity helps you keep fighting. You have a healing pool of four d12s that you can use on yourself. You can take a Bonus Action to expend dice from the pool and roll them, regaining Hit Points equal to the total rolled. All expended dice return to the pool when you finish a Long Rest. The pool holds one more die once you reach certain Barbarian levels: 5 dice at level 6, 6 dice at level 12, and 7 dice at level 17.", "Path of the Zealot|Fanatical Focus": "Once per active Rage, if a saving throw you make fails, you can roll it again and add a bonus equal to your Rage Damage bonus. You must use the new roll.", "Path of the Zealot|Zealous Presence": "As a Bonus Action, you let out a battle cry filled with divine energy. Choose up to ten other creatures within 60 feet of you. Each of them has Advantage on attack rolls and saving throws until your next turn starts. You can use this feature once per Long Rest. Spending one use of your Rage (no action required) also restores your use of it.", "Path of the Zealot|Rage of the Gods": "When you activate your Rage, you can transform into a divine warrior. You keep this form for 1 minute, or until your Hit Points fall to 0. You can use this feature once per Long Rest. The form grants you the following benefits. **Flight.** You can hover, and you have a Fly Speed that matches your Speed. **Resistance.** You gain Resistance to Necrotic damage, Psychic damage, and Radiant damage. **Revivification.** When a creature that is within 30 feet of you is about to drop to 0 Hit Points, you can use your Reaction and expend one use of your Rage to make its Hit Points equal to your Barbarian level instead.", "College of Dance|Dazzling Footwork": "You gain these benefits as long as you wear no armor and wield no Shield. **Dance Virtuoso.** You make any Charisma (Performance) check that involves your dancing with Advantage. **Unarmored Defense.** Your base Armor Class equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier. **Agile Strikes.** When an action, a Bonus Action, or a Reaction of yours includes expending a use of your Bardic Inspiration, you can also make one Unarmed Strike as part of it. **Bardic Damage.** Your Unarmed Strikes can use Dexterity in place of Strength for their attack rolls. When an Unarmed Strike deals damage, you can swap its normal damage for Bludgeoning damage that equals your Dexterity modifier + one roll of your Bardic Inspiration die. Rolling for this doesn't expend the die.", "College of Dance|Inspiring Movement": "If an enemy you can see is within 5 feet of you when it ends its turn, you can respond with a Reaction and spend one use of your Bardic Inspiration. You then move a distance of up to half your Speed. After that, you can pick one ally within 30 feet of you, and that ally can spend its Reaction to move up to half its Speed as well. No movement from this feature provokes Opportunity Attacks.", "College of Dance|Tandem Footwork": "As you roll Initiative, you can expend one use of Bardic Inspiration, as long as you don't have the Incapacitated condition. If you spend it, roll that Bardic Inspiration die. The number rolled becomes a bonus to Initiative for you and for each ally who is within 30 feet of you and can see or hear you.", "College of Dance|Leading Evasion": "When an effect lets you attempt a Dexterity saving throw to halve its damage, success on the save means you take no damage, and failure means you take only half damage. You can extend this benefit for that save to any creatures within 5 feet of you that are making the same Dexterity saving throw. This feature doesn't work while you have the Incapacitated condition.", "College of Glamour|Beguiling Magic": "Charm Person and Mirror Image are always prepared for you. Also, right after you use a spell slot to cast an Enchantment or Illusion spell, you can target one creature within 60 feet of you that you can see. That creature attempts a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. If it fails, it has the Charmed or Frightened condition (you choose which) for 1 minute. The target makes the save again as each of its turns ends, and the effect on it ends when it succeeds. You can use this benefit once per Long Rest. Spending one use of your Bardic Inspiration (no action required) also restores your use of it.", "College of Glamour|Mantle of Inspiration": "You can blend fey magic into a song or dance to invigorate others. You can take a Bonus Action to spend one use of Bardic Inspiration and roll the die. Then pick other creatures within 60 feet of you. The most you can pick equals your Charisma modifier (minimum 1). Each chosen creature gains twice the number you rolled as Temporary Hit Points. Each of them can then spend its Reaction to move as far as its Speed, and this movement provokes no Opportunity Attacks.", "College of Glamour|Mantle of Majesty": "Command is always prepared for you. Using a Bonus Action, you cast Command with no spell slot, and you gain an unearthly appearance that lasts 1 minute or until your Concentration ends. Until the appearance ends, you can also cast Command as a Bonus Action with no spell slot. Any creature you have Charmed automatically fails its saving throw against a Command you cast with this feature. You can use this feature once per Long Rest. Expending a level 3+ spell slot (no action required) also restores your use of it.", "College of Glamour|Unbreakable Majesty": "You can take a Bonus Action to assume a magically majestic presence. It lasts 1 minute or until you have the Incapacitated condition. Meanwhile, the first time on a turn that any creature hits you with an attack roll, the attacker makes a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC, and its attack misses instead if the save fails, as the creature recoils from your majesty. You can assume this presence once per Short or Long Rest.", "College of Lore|Bonus Proficiencies": "Choose any three skills. You gain proficiency in them.", "College of Lore|Cutting Words": "With your wit, you can supernaturally distract and confuse others or otherwise drain their confidence and competence. Whenever a creature within 60 feet of you succeeds on an attack roll or ability check, or makes a damage roll, and you can see that creature, you can take a Reaction and spend one use of your Bardic Inspiration. Roll that die and subtract the number from the creature's roll, which reduces the damage or might turn the success into a failure.", "College of Lore|Magical Discoveries": "You learn two spells of your choice, taken from the Cleric, Druid, or Wizard spell list in any combination. Each must be either a cantrip or a spell of a level you have spell slots for, according to the Bard Features table. The chosen spells are always prepared for you. Whenever you gain a Bard level, you can swap one of them for another spell that meets the same requirements.", "College of Lore|Peerless Skill": "If you fail an ability check or attack roll, you can spend one use of Bardic Inspiration. Add a roll of the Bardic Inspiration die to the d20, which might turn the failure into a success. If the roll still fails, that use of Bardic Inspiration isn't spent.", "College of Valor|Combat Inspiration": "Your wit can turn the tide of battle. A creature holding one of your Bardic Inspiration dice can spend it on one of the effects below. **Defense.** When an attack roll hits the creature, it can take a Reaction to roll the die and add the result to its Armor Class against that attack, which might cause the attack to miss. **Offense.** As soon as the creature's attack roll hits a target, the creature can add a roll of the die to the damage that attack deals to that target.", "College of Valor|Martial Training": "You become proficient with Martial weapons and gain training with Medium armor and Shields. You can also cast spells from your Bard spell list using a Simple or Martial weapon as your Spellcasting Focus.", "College of Valor|Extra Attack": "Taking the Attack action on your turn lets you attack two times instead of once. Instead of making one of those attacks, you can cast one of your cantrips whose casting time is an action.", "College of Valor|Battle Magic": "After you cast a spell whose casting time is an action, you can make one weapon attack as a Bonus Action.", "Life Domain|Disciple of Life": "If a creature regains Hit Points from a spell you cast using a spell slot, it also regains extra Hit Points on the same turn you cast the spell. The extra amount is 2 + the spell slot's level.", "Life Domain|Life Domain Spells": "Your bond with this divine domain keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Cleric level listed below, the spells for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Aid, Bless, Cure Wounds, Lesser Restoration. Level 5: Mass Healing Word, Revivify. Level 7: Aura of Life, Death Ward. Level 9: Greater Restoration, Mass Cure Wounds.", "Life Domain|Preserve Life": "Taking a Magic action, you hold up your Holy Symbol and spend one use of your Channel Divinity to call forth healing energy. The energy can restore Hit Points totaling five times your Cleric level. Divide them among any Bloodied creatures you choose within 30 feet of you, which can include yourself. This feature can't restore a creature to more than half its Hit Point maximum.", "Life Domain|Blessed Healer": "Healing spells you cast on others heal you too. Right after you use a spell slot to cast a spell that restores Hit Points to at least one creature other than you, you regain Hit Points equal to 2 + the spell slot's level.", "Life Domain|Supreme Healing": "When a spell or Channel Divinity of yours would have you roll one or more dice to restore a creature's Hit Points, don't roll them. Use the highest possible number on each die for that healing instead. For example, a spell that would restore 2d6 Hit Points to a creature restores 12 instead.", "Light Domain|Light Domain Spells": "Your bond with this divine domain keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Cleric level listed below, the spells for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Burning Hands, Faerie Fire, Scorching Ray, See Invisibility. Level 5: Daylight, Fireball. Level 7: Arcane Eye, Wall of Fire. Level 9: Flame Strike, Scrying.", "Light Domain|Radiance of the Dawn": "Taking a Magic action, you hold up your Holy Symbol and spend one use of your Channel Divinity, releasing a flash of light in a 30-foot Emanation from you. The flash dispels any magical Darkness in that area, such as Darkness made by the Darkness spell. Each creature of your choice in the area also makes a Constitution saving throw. A creature that fails takes Radiant damage equal to 2d10 + your Cleric level, and one that succeeds takes half as much.", "Light Domain|Warding Flare": "When a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see makes an attack roll, you can use your Reaction to impose Disadvantage on that roll, with light flaring before it hits or misses. Your uses of this feature equal your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and all expended uses return when you finish a Long Rest.", "Light Domain|Improved Warding Flare": "Finishing a Short or Long Rest now restores all expended uses of your Warding Flare. Also, each time you use Warding Flare, you can grant Temporary Hit Points equal to 2d6 + your Wisdom modifier to the target of the triggering attack.", "Light Domain|Corona of Light": "As a Magic action, you surround yourself with an aura of sunlight that lasts 1 minute. You can dismiss the aura earlier (no action required). It sheds Bright Light in a 60-foot radius around you and Dim Light for 30 feet past that. While your enemies are in the Bright Light, they make saving throws with Disadvantage against your Radiance of the Dawn and against spells that deal Fire or Radiant damage. Your uses of this feature equal your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and you get back every expended use when you finish a Long Rest.", "Trickery Domain|Blessing of the Trickster": "As a Magic action, you can grant Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to yourself or to one willing creature within 30 feet of you. The effect ends when you finish a Long Rest or use this feature again.", "Trickery Domain|Invoke Duplicity": "You can take a Bonus Action and expend one use of your Channel Divinity, which creates a perfect visual illusion of yourself. It appears in an unoccupied space you can see no more than 30 feet away from you. The illusion is intangible and doesn't take up its space. It remains for 1 minute, though it ends sooner if you dismiss it (no action required) or you have the Incapacitated condition. The illusion is animated and copies your expressions and gestures. For as long as it remains, you gain the following benefits. **Cast Spells.** You can cast spells as though you were standing in the illusion's space, but you must rely on your own senses. **Distract.** If you and your illusion are both within 5 feet of a creature able to see the illusion, the illusion distracts that creature so much that you have Advantage on attack rolls against it. **Move.** You can take a Bonus Action to shift the illusion as far as 30 feet, into an unoccupied space within 120 feet of you that you can see.", "Trickery Domain|Trickery Domain Spells": "Your bond with this divine domain keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Cleric level listed below, the spells for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Charm Person, Disguise Self, Invisibility, and Pass without Trace. Level 5: Hypnotic Pattern and Nondetection. Level 7: Confusion and Dimension Door. Level 9: Dominate Person and Modify Memory.", "Trickery Domain|Trickster's Transposition": "Each time you take the Bonus Action to create or move your Invoke Duplicity illusion, you can teleport so that you and the illusion trade places.", "Trickery Domain|Improved Duplicity": "The illusion from your Invoke Duplicity grows stronger in the following ways. **Shared Distraction.** Attack rolls made by you and your allies against any creature within 5 feet of the illusion have Advantage. **Healing Illusion.** Once the illusion ends, you or one creature you choose within 5 feet of it regains Hit Points equal to your Cleric level.", "War Domain|Guided Strike": "When an attack roll made by you or by a creature within 30 feet of you misses, you can spend one use of your Channel Divinity to add +10 to that roll, possibly turning it into a hit. If you use this feature for another creature's attack roll, it costs your Reaction.", "War Domain|War Domain Spells": "Your bond with this divine domain keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Cleric level listed below, the spells for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Guiding Bolt, Magic Weapon, Shield of Faith, and Spiritual Weapon. Level 5: Crusader's Mantle and Spirit Guardians. Level 7: Fire Shield and Freedom of Movement. Level 9: Hold Monster and Steel Wind Strike.", "War Domain|War Priest": "Using a Bonus Action, you can attack one time with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike. Your number of uses equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and finishing a Short or Long Rest restores all expended uses.", "War Domain|War God's Blessing": "Shield of Faith and Spiritual Weapon can be cast by expending a use of your Channel Divinity rather than a spell slot. When cast this way, either spell doesn't require Concentration. It lasts for 1 minute instead, but ends sooner if you cast that same spell again, have the Incapacitated condition, or die.", "War Domain|Avatar of Battle": "You gain Resistance against three damage types: Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing.", "Circle of the Land|Circle of the Land Spells": "Each time you finish a Long Rest, pick one type of land: arid, polar, temperate, or tropical. Look at the list below for that land. You have the spells shown for your Druid level and every lower level prepared. **Arid Land.** Level 3: Blur, Burning Hands, Fire Bolt. Level 5: Fireball. Level 7: Blight. Level 9: Wall of Stone. **Polar Land.** Level 3: Fog Cloud, Hold Person, Ray of Frost. Level 5: Sleet Storm. Level 7: Ice Storm. Level 9: Cone of Cold. **Temperate Land.** Level 3: Misty Step, Shocking Grasp, Sleep. Level 5: Lightning Bolt. Level 7: Freedom of Movement. Level 9: Tree Stride. **Tropical Land.** Level 3: Acid Splash, Ray of Sickness, Web. Level 5: Stinking Cloud. Level 7: Polymorph. Level 9: Insect Plague.", "Circle of the Land|Land's Aid": "You can take a Magic action and expend one use of Wild Shape to target a point within 60 feet of you. Flowers that grant vitality and thorns that drain life briefly sprout in a Sphere with a 10-foot radius, centered on that point. Every creature you choose in the Sphere attempts a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC. Failing the save deals 2d6 Necrotic damage to the creature, and succeeding halves that damage. Also, one creature you choose in the area regains 2d6 Hit Points. Both the damage and the healing grow by 1d6 at Druid levels 10 (3d6) and 14 (4d6).", "Circle of the Land|Natural Recovery": "You can cast one level 1+ spell that you have prepared through your Circle Spells feature without expending a spell slot. After you do, you must finish a Long Rest before casting a spell this way again. Also, when you finish a Short Rest, you can pick expended spell slots to recover. Their combined level can be no more than half your Druid level (rounded up), and none of them can be level 6 or higher. For example, a level 6 Druid can recover up to three levels' worth of slots: one level 3 slot, a level 2 slot and a level 1 slot, or three level 1 slots. You can recover spell slots with this feature only once per Long Rest.", "Circle of the Land|Nature's Ward": "You are immune to the Poisoned condition. You also have Resistance to the damage type tied to the land you currently have chosen for your Circle Spells feature: Fire for arid, Cold for polar, Lightning for temperate, or Poison for tropical.", "Circle of the Land|Nature's Sanctuary": "You can take a Magic action and expend one use of Wild Shape to summon spectral trees and vines. Choose a spot on the ground within 120 feet of you. The trees and vines fill a 15-foot Cube there and stay for 1 minute, or until you die or have the Incapacitated condition. Inside that area, you and your allies have Half Cover, and your allies also gain whatever Resistance your Nature's Ward currently gives you. You can take a Bonus Action to shift the Cube up to 60 feet, onto ground within 120 feet of you.", "Circle of the Moon|Circle Forms": "Whenever you assume a Wild Shape form, you can draw on lunar magic to gain the following benefits. **Challenge Rating.** The highest Challenge Rating the form can have is your Druid level divided by 3 (rounded down). **Armor Class.** Until you leave the form, your Armor Class is 13 + your Wisdom modifier whenever that total beats the Beast's Armor Class. **Temporary Hit Points.** You gain a number of Temporary Hit Points that is three times your Druid level.", "Circle of the Moon|Circle of the Moon Spells": "Once you reach a Druid level listed below, the spells for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Cure Wounds, Moonbeam, and Starry Wisp. Level 5: Conjure Animals. Level 7: Fount of Moonlight. Level 9: Mass Cure Wounds. You can also cast the spells from this feature while you are in a Wild Shape form.", "Circle of the Moon|Improved Circle Forms": "These benefits apply to you whenever you are in a Wild Shape form. **Lunar Radiance.** Every attack you make in a Wild Shape form can deal either its usual damage type or Radiant damage, and you decide which each time one of those attacks hits. **Increased Toughness.** You can add a bonus equal to your Wisdom modifier to your Constitution saving throws.", "Circle of the Moon|Moonlight Step": "You can magically transport yourself, appearing again amid a burst of moonlight. To do so, take a Bonus Action and teleport to an unoccupied space you can see up to 30 feet away. Until this turn ends, your next attack roll has Advantage. Your uses of this feature equal your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and a Long Rest restores all expended uses. Expending a level 2+ spell slot (no action required) also restores one use per slot.", "Circle of the Moon|Lunar Form": "Lunar power suffuses you, giving you these benefits. **Improved Lunar Radiance.** When a Wild Shape form's attack of yours hits a target, you can deal an extra 2d10 Radiant damage to that target, but only once per turn. **Shared Moonlight.** Each time you use Moonlight Step, you can bring along one willing creature within 10 feet of you by teleporting it too. It arrives in an unoccupied space that you can see, no farther than 10 feet from where you arrive.", "Circle of the Sea|Circle of the Sea Spells": "Once you reach a Druid level listed below, the spells for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Fog Cloud, Gust of Wind, Ray of Frost, Thunderwave, and Shatter. Level 5: Lightning Bolt and Water Breathing. Level 7: Control Water and Ice Storm. Level 9: Conjure Elemental and Hold Monster.", "Circle of the Sea|Wrath of the Sea": "You can take a Bonus Action and expend one use of Wild Shape to wrap yourself in ocean spray, a 5-foot Emanation that lasts 10 minutes. The spray ends early if you dismiss it (no action required), if you manifest it again, or if you have the Incapacitated condition. As you manifest it, and again as a Bonus Action on each later turn, you can target another creature in the Emanation that you can see. That creature attempts a Constitution saving throw against your spell save DC, and it takes Cold damage if it fails. A failing target that is Large or smaller is also pushed up to 15 feet away from you. To find the damage, roll d6s equal in number to your Wisdom modifier (minimum of one die).", "Circle of the Sea|Aquatic Affinity": "The Emanation from your Wrath of the Sea grows to 10 feet. You also gain a Swim Speed that equals your Speed.", "Circle of the Sea|Stormborn": "Two more benefits apply while your Wrath of the Sea is active. **Flight.** You gain a Fly Speed that equals your Speed. **Resistance.** You gain Resistance to Cold damage, Lightning damage, and Thunder damage.", "Circle of the Sea|Oceanic Gift": "When you create the Emanation of your Wrath of the Sea, you can center it on one willing creature within 60 feet of you rather than on yourself. That creature gets every benefit of the Emanation, and it uses your spell save DC and your Wisdom modifier for it. Alternatively, by spending two of your Wild Shape uses rather than one when you create the Emanation, you can make it surround both that creature and you.", "Circle of the Stars|Star Map": "As part of your study of the heavens, you have made a star chart. It is a Tiny object, and it can serve as a Spellcasting Focus for your Druid spells. Pick its form or roll 1d6 on the Star Map table: 1, a scroll showing constellations; 2, a stone tablet pierced by fine drilled holes; 3, an owlbear hide worked with stellar symbols; 4, a set of maps inside an ebony binding; 5, a crystal carved with starry patterns; 6, a glass disk with constellations etched into it. While you hold the map, Guidance and Guiding Bolt are both prepared for you, and you can also cast Guiding Bolt with no spell slot. Your number of such castings equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and finishing a Long Rest restores all expended uses. If the map is lost, a 1-hour ceremony lets you magically create a new one. This ceremony can take place as part of a Short or Long Rest, and completing it destroys the old map.", "Circle of the Stars|Starry Form": "As a Bonus Action, you can spend one of your Wild Shape uses to take on a starry form rather than change shape. In this form you keep your game statistics, but your body turns luminous, your joints shine like stars, and glowing lines link them as on a star chart. Bright Light spreads from the form in a 10-foot radius, with Dim Light reaching 10 feet farther. The form lasts 10 minutes. It ends sooner if you use this feature again, if you have the Incapacitated condition, or if you dismiss it (no action required). Each time you take on the starry form, choose which of the constellations below glimmers on your body. The one you choose sets the benefits you get while in the form. **Archer.** An archer constellation appears on you. When you activate the form, and as a Bonus Action on later turns while it lasts, you can hurl a luminous arrow by making a ranged spell attack against one creature within 60 feet of you. If the arrow hits, the target takes 1d8 plus your Wisdom modifier in Radiant damage. **Chalice.** You bear a constellation shaped like a goblet that gives life. Each time you cast a spell with a spell slot and the spell restores Hit Points to any creature, you can pick yourself or another creature within 30 feet of you, and that creature regains Hit Points equal to 1d8 plus your Wisdom modifier. **Dragon.** A wise dragon constellation appears on you. On an Intelligence check, a Wisdom check, or a Constitution saving throw made to keep Concentration, you can count any d20 roll of 9 or lower as a 10.", "Circle of the Stars|Cosmic Omen": "Each time you finish a Long Rest, you can read omens in your Star Map and roll a die. Whether the number is even or odd decides which special Reaction you have until you finish your next Long Rest. **Weal (Even).** Just before a creature makes a D20 Test, if it is within 30 feet of you and you can see it, you can use your Reaction to roll 1d6 and add the number to its total. **Woe (Odd).** Just before a creature makes a D20 Test, if it is within 30 feet of you and you can see it, you can use your Reaction to roll 1d6 and subtract the number from its total. Your number of uses of this Reaction equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and finishing a Long Rest restores all expended uses.", "Circle of the Stars|Twinkling Constellations": "The constellations of your Starry Form grow stronger. The Archer and the Chalice each use 2d8 in place of 1d8. When the Dragon is the active constellation, you gain a Fly Speed of 20 feet and can hover. Also, at the start of each of your turns in your Starry Form, you can switch which constellation glimmers on your body.", "Circle of the Stars|Full of Stars": "While you are in your Starry Form, your body becomes partly incorporeal. This gives you Resistance to Slashing, Piercing, and Bludgeoning damage.", "Battle Master|Combat Superiority": "Your time on the battlefield has sharpened your fighting techniques. You learn maneuvers, which are powered by special dice known as Superiority Dice. **Maneuvers.** Choose three maneuvers to learn from the Maneuver Options section of this subclass. Many maneuvers enhance an attack somehow. Only one maneuver can be used on any single attack. When you reach Fighter levels 7, 10, and 15, you learn two more maneuvers of your choice. Whenever you learn new maneuvers, you can also swap one maneuver you know for a different one. **Superiority Dice.** You start with four Superiority Dice, and each is a d8. Using a Superiority Die expends it. Finishing a Short or Long Rest restores all your expended Superiority Dice. You gain one more Superiority Die at Fighter level 7 (five dice total) and another at Fighter level 15 (six dice total). **Saving Throws.** For a maneuver that requires a saving throw, the DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your choice of your Strength or Dexterity modifier.", "Battle Master|Student of War": "Choose one type of Artisan's Tools and gain proficiency with it. Also choose one skill from those offered to Fighters at level 1 and gain proficiency in it.", "Battle Master|Know Your Enemy": "As a Bonus Action, choose a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, and discern certain of its strengths and weaknesses. You learn whether it has any Immunities, Resistances, or Vulnerabilities, and if it has any, you also learn what they are. Once you use this feature, you must finish a Long Rest before using it again, though expending one Superiority Die (no action required) also restores a use.", "Battle Master|Improved Combat Superiority": "Your Superiority Dice are now d10s.", "Battle Master|Relentless": "Once per turn, you can fuel a maneuver with a 1d8 roll rather than a Superiority Die. Roll the 1d8 and use its result in place of the die, and no Superiority Die is expended.", "Battle Master|Ultimate Combat Superiority": "Your Superiority Dice are now d12s.", "Champion|Improved Critical": "A d20 roll of 19 or 20 can score a Critical Hit for any attack roll you make with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike.", "Champion|Remarkable Athlete": "Your athletic skill gives you Advantage on Initiative rolls and on Strength (Athletics) checks. Also, right after you score a Critical Hit, you can move a distance up to half your Speed, and this movement doesn't provoke Opportunity Attacks.", "Champion|Additional Fighting Style": "Choose one more Fighting Style feat and gain it.", "Champion|Heroic Warrior": "The thrill of battle pushes you on toward victory. In combat, whenever you start your turn without Heroic Inspiration, you can give it to yourself.", "Champion|Superior Critical": "A d20 roll of 18, 19, or 20 can now score a Critical Hit for any attack roll you make with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike.", "Champion|Survivor": "You reach the peak of toughness in battle and gain the benefits below. **Defy Death.** Your Death Saving Throws have Advantage. Also, a roll of 18 to 20 on a Death Saving Throw gives you the same benefit as rolling a 20. **Heroic Rally.** When each of your turns begins while you are Bloodied but still have 1 or more Hit Points, you regain Hit Points equal to your Constitution modifier plus 5.", "Eldritch Knight|Spellcasting": "You have learned to cast spells. Chapter 7 has the rules for spellcasting, and the details below show how you use them as an Eldritch Knight. **Cantrips.** Choose two cantrips from the Wizard spell list. You know them. Ray of Frost and Shocking Grasp are suggested. Each time you gain a Fighter level, you can trade one of these cantrips for a different Wizard cantrip you choose. Upon reaching Fighter level 10, you learn another Wizard cantrip you choose. **Spell Slots.** Your spell slots for casting level 1+ spells appear in the Eldritch Knight Spellcasting table. Every expended slot comes back after you finish a Long Rest. The table grants these slots. Level 1 slots: two at Fighter level 3, three at Fighter levels 4 to 6, and four from Fighter level 7 onward. Level 2 slots: two at Fighter levels 7 to 9, and three from Fighter level 10 onward. Level 3 slots: two at Fighter levels 13 to 15, and three from Fighter level 16 onward. Level 4 slots: one at Fighter levels 19 and 20. **Prepared Spells of Level 1+.** Your list of prepared level 1+ spells holds the spells you can cast with this feature. Start the list with three level 1 Wizard spells. Burning Hands, Jump, and Shield are suggested. The list gets longer as your Fighter level rises, following the Prepared Spells column of that table. That column lists 3 spells at Fighter level 3, 4 at levels 4 to 6, 5 at level 7, 6 at levels 8 and 9, 7 at level 10, 8 at levels 11 and 12, 9 at level 13, 10 at levels 14 and 15, 11 at levels 16 to 18, 12 at level 19, and 13 at level 20. Whenever the number rises, add Wizard spells until the size of your list matches the table. Every spell you choose has to be of a level you have spell slots for. For instance, a level 7 Fighter can have five Wizard spells on the list, mixing level 1 and level 2 spells in any way. **Changing Your Prepared Spells.** When you gain a Fighter level, you can take one spell off your list and put another Wizard spell of a level you have spell slots for in its place. **Spellcasting Ability.** You use Intelligence as the spellcasting ability for your Wizard spells. **Spellcasting Focus.** For your Wizard spells, an Arcane Focus can serve as your Spellcasting Focus.", "Eldritch Knight|War Bond": "You learn a ritual that forms a magical bond between you and one weapon. The ritual takes 1 hour, and you can perform it during a Short Rest. The weapon must stay within your reach for the whole ritual, and when the ritual ends, you touch the weapon and the bond is forged. No bond forms when the weapon already has a bond with another Fighter, or when it is a magic item that someone else is attuned to. After you bond a weapon to yourself, no one can disarm you of it unless you have the Incapacitated condition. If the weapon is on your plane of existence, you can take a Bonus Action to summon it, and it teleports instantly into your hand. Two bonded weapons is your maximum, and each Bonus Action summons just one of them. If you try to bond with a third weapon, you must break your bond with one of the other two.", "Eldritch Knight|War Magic": "On your turn, if you take the Attack action, you can trade one of its attacks for casting one of your Wizard cantrips that takes an action to cast.", "Eldritch Knight|Eldritch Strike": "Your weapon strikes now undermine a creature's ability to withstand your spells. If an attack you make with a weapon hits a creature, that creature's next saving throw against a spell you cast before your next turn is over is made with Disadvantage.", "Eldritch Knight|Arcane Charge": "Each time you use Action Surge, you can also teleport up to 30 feet into an unoccupied space that you can see. The teleport can happen before or after the extra action.", "Eldritch Knight|Improved War Magic": "On your turn, if you take the Attack action, you can trade two of its attacks to cast a level 1 or level 2 Wizard spell of yours whose casting time is an action.", "Psi Warrior|Psionic Power": "You carry a wellspring of psionic energy, represented by your Psionic Energy Dice. These dice fuel the powers this subclass grants. The Psi Warrior Energy Dice table gives their size and number by Fighter level: four d6s at level 3, six d8s at level 5, eight d8s at level 9, eight d10s at level 11, ten d10s at level 13, and twelve d12s at level 17. A feature of this subclass that uses a Psionic Energy Die can use only the dice from this subclass. Some powers expend a die, as their descriptions say, and a power that needs a die can't be used once all your Psionic Energy Dice are expended. Finishing a Short Rest restores one expended Psionic Energy Die, and finishing a Long Rest restores all of them. **Protective Field.** Whenever damage is dealt to you or to another creature within 30 feet of you that you can see, you can use your Reaction to expend one Psionic Energy Die. Roll it, and a brief shield of telekinetic force reduces the damage by the roll plus your Intelligence modifier (the damage drops by at least 1). **Psionic Strike.** Psionic force can propel your weapons. Once on each of your turns, immediately after an attack you make with a weapon hits a target within 30 feet of you and deals damage to it, you can spend one Psionic Energy Die. Roll it, and the target takes Force damage equal to the roll plus your Intelligence modifier. **Telekinetic Movement.** Your mind can move an object or a creature. As a Magic action, pick one target within 30 feet of you that you can see: it must be a loose object no bigger than Large, or a willing creature that isn't you. You move the target up to 30 feet into an unoccupied space you can see. If the target is a Tiny object, you can instead move it into your hand or out of it. After you take this action, it stays unavailable to you until you finish a Short or Long Rest, though spending a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) restores your use of it.", "Psi Warrior|Telekinetic Adept": "You now command new uses of your telekinetic abilities, as follows. **Psi-Powered Leap.** You can take a Bonus Action to gain a Fly Speed that is twice your Speed, lasting until the current turn ends. Once you take this Bonus Action, it stays unavailable to you until you finish a Short or Long Rest, though spending a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) restores your use of it. **Telekinetic Thrust.** Whenever your Psionic Strike damages a target, you can choose to subject the target to a Strength saving throw. The DC equals 8 plus your Intelligence modifier and your Proficiency Bonus. If the target fails, you can either give it the Prone condition or move it up to 10 feet horizontally.", "Psi Warrior|Guarded Mind": "You gain Resistance to Psychic damage. Also, if your turn begins while you have the Charmed or Frightened condition, you can spend one Psionic Energy Die, with no action required, to end every effect on yourself that is causing those conditions.", "Psi Warrior|Bulwark of Force": "Telekinetic force lets you shield yourself and others. As a Bonus Action, choose creatures within 30 feet of you, yourself included if you like. The number of creatures can't exceed your Intelligence modifier (minimum of one creature), and each of them has Half Cover. The cover lasts 1 minute and ends early if you have the Incapacitated condition. After you use this feature, it stays unavailable to you until you finish a Long Rest, though spending a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) restores your use of it.", "Psi Warrior|Telekinetic Master": "The Telekinesis spell is always prepared for you. With this feature you can cast it with no spell slot and no components, using Intelligence as your spellcasting ability for it. On each of your turns while you keep Concentration on it, the turn you cast it included, you can take a Bonus Action to make one attack with a weapon. Once you cast the spell through this feature, you can't cast it that way again until you finish a Long Rest, though spending a Psionic Energy Die (no action required) restores your use of it.", "Warrior of Mercy|Hand of Harm": "Once per turn, when your Unarmed Strike hits a creature and deals damage, you can spend 1 Focus Point to add Necrotic damage to it. The extra damage equals your Wisdom modifier plus one roll of your Martial Arts die.", "Warrior of Mercy|Hand of Healing": "As a Magic action, you can spend 1 Focus Point and touch a creature. It regains Hit Points equal to your Wisdom modifier plus a roll of your Martial Arts die. Whenever you use Flurry of Blows, one of its Unarmed Strikes can be replaced by a use of this feature, and that healing costs you no Focus Point.", "Warrior of Mercy|Implements of Mercy": "You become proficient in the Insight and Medicine skills, and you also gain proficiency with the Herbalism Kit.", "Warrior of Mercy|Physician's Touch": "Two of your features grow stronger, as described below. **Hand of Harm.** Each time Hand of Harm affects a creature, you can also inflict the Poisoned condition on that creature until your next turn ends. **Hand of Healing.** Each time Hand of Healing heals a creature, you can also remove one of these conditions from it: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, or Stunned.", "Warrior of Mercy|Flurry of Healing and Harm": "When you use Flurry of Blows, you can swap each of its Unarmed Strikes for a use of Hand of Healing, and the healing costs you no Focus Points. Also, when an Unarmed Strike from Flurry of Blows deals damage, you can apply Hand of Harm to that strike without paying a Focus Point for Hand of Harm. You are still limited to one use of Hand of Harm per turn. Your total uses of these benefits equal your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and finishing a Long Rest restores all expended uses.", "Warrior of Mercy|Hand of Ultimate Mercy": "Your mastery of life energy opens the way to ultimate mercy. You can take a Magic action to spend 5 Focus Points and touch the body of a dead creature, if it died no more than 24 hours ago. The creature comes back to life with Hit Points equal to your Wisdom modifier plus 4d10. If it had any of these conditions when it died, it revives without them: Blinded, Deafened, Paralyzed, Poisoned, and Stunned. After you use this feature, it is unavailable to you until you finish a Long Rest.", "Warrior of Shadow|Shadow Arts": "You have learned to tap the power of the Shadowfell, which grants you the benefits below. **Darkness.** You can spend 1 Focus Point to cast the Darkness spell with no spell components. When you cast it this way, you can see inside the spell's area. For as long as the spell lasts, you can move its area of Darkness at the start of each of your turns to a space within 60 feet of you. **Darkvision.** You gain Darkvision with a 60-foot range. If you already have it, add 60 feet to its range. **Shadowy Figments.** Minor Illusion is a spell you know, and Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.", "Warrior of Shadow|Shadow Step": "If you are entirely within Dim Light or Darkness, you can take a Bonus Action to teleport to an unoccupied space within 60 feet that you can see and that is also in Dim Light or Darkness. After you teleport, your next melee attack before the current turn ends has Advantage.", "Warrior of Shadow|Improved Shadow Step": "Your link to the Shadowfell strengthens your teleportation. When you use Shadow Step, you can spend 1 Focus Point so that, for that use, you don't need to start and end in Dim Light or Darkness. As part of this Bonus Action, you can also make an Unarmed Strike right after you teleport.", "Warrior of Shadow|Cloak of Shadows": "While you are entirely within Dim Light or Darkness, you can take a Magic action and spend 3 Focus Points to wrap yourself in shadows. The shadows end after 1 minute, when you have the Incapacitated condition, or when you end your turn in Bright Light. While the shadows cover you, you gain the benefits below. **Invisibility.** The Invisible condition applies to you. **Partially Incorporeal.** Occupied spaces don't block you, since you can move through them as though they were Difficult Terrain. Should your turn end in such a space, you are moved back to the unoccupied space you were last in. **Shadow Flurry.** Your Flurry of Blows costs you no Focus Points.", "Warrior of the Elements|Elemental Attunement": "When your turn starts, you can spend 1 Focus Point to fill yourself with elemental energy. The energy lasts 10 minutes or until you have the Incapacitated condition. While this feature is active, you gain the benefits below. **Reach.** Elemental energy extends from you, so your reach with an Unarmed Strike is 10 feet longer than normal. **Elemental Strikes.** Each time your Unarmed Strike hits, you can have it deal Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage (your choice) in place of its normal damage type. When it deals one of these types, you can also make the target attempt a Strength saving throw. If the target fails, elemental energy swirls around it, and you can move it up to 10 feet toward you or away from you.", "Warrior of the Elements|Manipulate Elements": "You know the Elementalism spell, and you use Wisdom as your spellcasting ability for it.", "Warrior of the Elements|Elemental Burst": "As a Magic action, you can spend 2 Focus Points and pick a point within 120 feet of you. Elemental energy bursts out in a 20-foot-radius Sphere centered there. Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder as the damage type. Each creature inside the Sphere must attempt a Dexterity saving throw. A creature that fails takes three rolls of your Martial Arts die in damage of the chosen type, and a creature that succeeds takes half as much.", "Warrior of the Elements|Stride of the Elements": "As long as your Elemental Attunement is active, you also gain a Fly Speed and a Swim Speed, each equal to your Speed.", "Warrior of the Elements|Elemental Epitome": "As long as your Elemental Attunement is active, you also gain the benefits below. **Damage Resistance.** Choose Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder damage. You gain Resistance to that type, and you can switch your choice at the start of each of your turns. **Destructive Stride.** Using your Step of the Wind raises your Speed by 20 feet until the turn ends. Until then, when you enter a space within 5 feet of any creature you choose, that creature takes one roll of your Martial Arts die as damage. You pick the damage type from Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Thunder. No creature can take this damage more than once per turn. **Empowered Strikes.** When you hit a target with an Unarmed Strike, you can roll your Martial Arts die once and deal that much extra damage to it. You can do this only once on each of your turns. The extra damage has the same type as the damage of that strike.", "Warrior of the Open Hand|Open Hand Technique": "Each time an attack granted by your Flurry of Blows hits a creature, you can apply one of the effects below to that target. **Addle.** The target loses the ability to make Opportunity Attacks until its next turn starts. **Push.** The target makes a Strength saving throw. On a failure, it is pushed as far as 15 feet away from you. **Topple.** The target makes a Dexterity saving throw. On a failure, it has the Prone condition.", "Warrior of the Open Hand|Wholeness of Body": "You can now heal yourself. You can take a Bonus Action to roll your Martial Arts die and regain Hit Points equal to the roll plus your Wisdom modifier (you regain at least 1 Hit Point). Your number of uses of this feature equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once). Finishing a Long Rest restores all expended uses.", "Warrior of the Open Hand|Fleet Step": "After any Bonus Action you take other than Step of the Wind, you can immediately use Step of the Wind as well.", "Warrior of the Open Hand|Quivering Palm": "You can now set up deadly vibrations in a creature's body. When your Unarmed Strike hits a creature, you can spend 4 Focus Points to start these unnoticeable vibrations. Their duration is a number of days equal to your Monk level. Until you take an action to end them, they do no harm. Rather than using an action, you can also end them on your turn by giving up one attack of your Attack action. You can end them only while you and the target are on the same plane of existence. Once ended, they force the target to make a Constitution saving throw. It takes 10d12 Force damage on a failure, or half as much on a success. Only one creature at a time can be under the effect of this feature. You can also end the vibrations harmlessly (no action required).", "Oath of Devotion|Oath of Devotion Spells": "Your oath's magic keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Paladin level shown in the Oath of Devotion Spells table, the spells listed for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Protection from Evil and Good, Shield of Faith. Level 5: Aid, Zone of Truth. Level 9: Beacon of Hope, Dispel Magic. Level 13: Freedom of Movement, Guardian of Faith. Level 17: Commune, Flame Strike.", "Oath of Devotion|Sacred Weapon": "As part of taking the Attack action, you can spend one use of Channel Divinity to charge one Melee weapon you are holding with positive energy. This lasts 10 minutes, ending sooner if you use this feature again. Until it ends, your attack rolls with that weapon gain a bonus equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum bonus of +1), and whenever the weapon hits, you decide whether it deals Radiant damage or its normal damage type. The weapon also sheds Bright Light out to 20 feet and Dim Light for another 20 feet. You can end the effect early (no action required). It also ends when you stop carrying the weapon.", "Oath of Devotion|Aura of Devotion": "Inside your Aura of Protection, the Charmed condition can't affect you or your allies, since you all have Immunity to it there. If an ally is already Charmed when it enters the aura, the condition does nothing to that ally for as long as it stays there.", "Oath of Devotion|Smite of Protection": "Your magical smite now gives off protective energy. Each time you cast Divine Smite, your Aura of Protection grants Half Cover to you and your allies while in it. This benefit lasts until your next turn starts.", "Oath of Devotion|Holy Nimbus": "As a Bonus Action, you can fill your Aura of Protection with holy power. It grants the benefits below for 10 minutes unless you end them sooner (no action required). After you use this feature, it is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest, though expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required) also restores your use of it. **Holy Ward.** Saving throws that a Fiend or an Undead forces you to make have Advantage for you. **Radiant Damage.** An enemy that starts its turn in the aura takes Radiant damage equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Charisma modifier. **Sunlight.** Bright Light that counts as sunlight fills the aura.", "Oath of Glory|Inspiring Smite": "Right after you cast Divine Smite, you can spend one use of Channel Divinity to give out Temporary Hit Points among creatures of your choice within 30 feet of you, yourself included if you wish. Roll 2d8 and add your Paladin level. That total is the number of Temporary Hit Points, divided among the chosen creatures however you like.", "Oath of Glory|Peerless Athlete": "As a Bonus Action, you can spend one use of Channel Divinity to heighten your athleticism. For 1 hour, you have Advantage on Dexterity (Acrobatics) and Strength (Athletics) checks, and your Long Jumps and High Jumps each reach 10 feet farther. This extra distance costs movement as normal.", "Oath of Glory|Oath of Glory Spells": "Your oath's magic keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Paladin level shown in the Oath of Glory Spells table, the spells listed for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Guiding Bolt, Heroism. Level 5: Enhance Ability, Magic Weapon. Level 9: Haste, Protection from Energy. Level 13: Compulsion, Freedom of Movement. Level 17: Legend Lore, Yolande's Regal Presence.", "Oath of Glory|Aura of Alacrity": "Your Speed increases by 10 feet. Also, an ally gains 10 feet of Speed, lasting until the end of its next turn, whenever it starts its turn in your Aura of Protection or enters the aura for the first time on a turn.", "Oath of Glory|Glorious Defense": "Your defense can become a sudden counterstrike. When an attack roll hits you, or hits a creature within 10 feet of you that you can see, you can take a Reaction to give the target a bonus to its Armor Class against that attack, which might make the attack miss. This bonus is your Charisma modifier, though never less than +1. Should the attack then miss, this same Reaction lets you make one weapon attack against the attacker, as long as the attacker is within your weapon's range. The number of times you can use this feature equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of once). Finishing a Long Rest restores all expended uses.", "Oath of Glory|Living Legend": "You can draw power from the legends of your great deeds, true or exaggerated. You can take a Bonus Action to gain the benefits below, which last 10 minutes. After you use this feature, it is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest, though expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required) also restores your use of it. **Charismatic.** Blessed with an otherworldly presence, you make all Charisma checks with Advantage. **Saving Throw Reroll.** After a failed saving throw, you can use your Reaction to reroll it, and you must keep the new result. **Unerring Strike.** When you miss with an attack roll made with a weapon, you can turn the miss into a hit. You can do this once on each of your turns.", "Oath of the Ancients|Nature's Wrath": "You can take a Magic action and spend one use of Channel Divinity to call up spectral vines around nearby creatures. Choose any creatures within 15 feet of you that you can see. Each one makes a Strength saving throw, and on a failure it has the Restrained condition for 1 minute. A creature Restrained this way makes the save again at the end of each of its turns, and a success ends the effect on it.", "Oath of the Ancients|Oath of the Ancients Spells": "Your oath's magic keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Paladin level shown in the Oath of the Ancients Spells table, the spells listed for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Ensnaring Strike, Speak with Animals. Level 5: Misty Step, Moonbeam. Level 9: Plant Growth, Protection from Energy. Level 13: Ice Storm, Stoneskin. Level 17: Commune with Nature, Tree Stride.", "Oath of the Ancients|Aura of Warding": "Ancient magic rests on you so heavily that it forms an eldritch ward, which blunts energy from beyond the Material Plane. While in your Aura of Protection, you and your allies gain Resistance to Necrotic, Psychic, and Radiant damage.", "Oath of the Ancients|Undying Sentinel": "If you drop to 0 Hit Points and aren't killed outright, you can go to 1 Hit Point instead, then regain a number of Hit Points equal to your Paladin level times three. After you use this feature, it is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest. Also, magic can't age you, and you stop visibly aging.", "Oath of the Ancients|Elder Champion": "As a Bonus Action, you can fill your Aura of Protection with primal power. It grants the benefits below for 1 minute unless you end them sooner (no action required). After you use this feature, it is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest, though expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required) also restores your use of it. **Diminish Defiance.** Enemies in the aura make saving throws against your spells and your Channel Divinity options with Disadvantage. **Regeneration.** You regain 10 Hit Points when each of your turns starts. **Swift Spells.** Any spell you cast that has a casting time of an action can be cast with a Bonus Action instead.", "Oath of Vengeance|Vow of Enmity": "When you take the Attack action, you can spend one use of Channel Divinity to swear a vow of enmity against a creature within 30 feet of you that you can see. Your attack rolls against that creature have Advantage, which lasts 1 minute or ends sooner if you use this feature again. If the creature falls to 0 Hit Points while the vow is still in effect, you can move the vow onto another creature that is within 30 feet of you (no action required).", "Oath of Vengeance|Oath of Vengeance Spells": "Your oath's magic keeps certain spells ready for you. Once you reach a Paladin level shown in the Oath of Vengeance Spells table, the spells listed for that level are always prepared for you from then on. Level 3: Bane, Hunter's Mark. Level 5: Hold Person, Misty Step. Level 9: Haste, Protection from Energy. Level 13: Banishment, Dimension Door. Level 17: Hold Monster, Scrying.", "Oath of Vengeance|Relentless Avenger": "Your supernatural focus lets you block an enemy's escape. When your Opportunity Attack hits a creature, you can reduce that creature's Speed to 0 until the current turn ends. As part of that same Reaction, you can then move a distance of up to half your Speed without provoking Opportunity Attacks.", "Oath of Vengeance|Soul of Vengeance": "When the creature that is subject to your Vow of Enmity makes an attack roll, you can take a Reaction right after that roll, whether it hit or missed, to make a melee attack against the creature if it is within range.", "Oath of Vengeance|Avenging Angel": "You can take a Bonus Action to gain the benefits below. They last 10 minutes unless you end them sooner (no action required). After you use this feature, it is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest, though expending a level 5 spell slot (no action required) also restores your use of it. **Flight.** Spectral wings sprout from your back, giving you a Fly Speed of 60 feet and the ability to hover. **Frightful Aura.** An enemy that starts its turn in your Aura of Protection makes a Wisdom saving throw. If it fails, it has the Frightened condition, which lasts 1 minute or until it takes any damage. While it is Frightened this way, attack rolls against it have Advantage.", "Beast Master|Primal Companion": "By magic, you summon a primal beast that draws strength from your bond with nature. Its stat block is your choice of Beast of the Sky, Beast of the Land, or Beast of the Sea. You also decide which kind of animal it is, picking one that suits that stat block. Whatever you pick, the beast bears primal markings that reveal its supernatural origin. It is Friendly to you and your allies, and it follows your commands. If you die, the beast vanishes. **The Beast in Combat.** During combat, the beast acts on your turn. It moves and uses its Reaction by itself, but the only action it takes is Dodge unless you use a Bonus Action to order it to take an action from its stat block or some other action. Also, when you take the Attack action, you can give up one of your attacks to order the beast to take its Beast's Strike action. While you have the Incapacitated condition, the beast acts independently and isn't restricted to Dodge. **Restoring or Replacing the Beast.** If the beast died no more than an hour ago, you can touch it as a Magic action and expend a spell slot. One minute later, it returns to life with every Hit Point restored. Each time you finish a Long Rest, you can summon another primal beast. It shows up in an unoccupied space no more than 5 feet away from you, and you pick its stat block and its appearance. Any beast you already have from this feature vanishes when the new one arrives.", "Beast Master|Exceptional Training": "Each time a Bonus Action of yours commands your Primal Companion beast to act, you can also have the beast use its own Bonus Action to take the Dash, Disengage, Dodge, or Help action. In addition, any time the beast hits with an attack roll and deals damage, that damage can be Force or its normal type, as you choose.", "Beast Master|Bestial Fury": "The beast can use the Beast's Strike action twice each time you command it to take that action. Also, the first time on each turn that the beast hits a creature affected by your Hunter's Mark spell, it deals extra Force damage equal to that spell's bonus damage.", "Beast Master|Share Spells": "If your Primal Companion beast is within 30 feet of you when you cast a spell that targets you, you can have the spell affect the beast too.", "Fey Wanderer|Dreadful Strikes": "Mind-scarring magic from the Feywild empowers your weapon strikes. Whenever you hit a creature with a weapon, you can have the hit deal an extra 1d4 Psychic damage to it. A given creature can take this extra damage no more than once per turn. Once you reach Ranger level 11, the extra damage becomes 1d6.", "Fey Wanderer|Otherworldly Glamour": "You add your Wisdom modifier (minimum of +1) as a bonus to every Charisma check you make. You also become proficient in one skill of your choice from Deception, Performance, and Persuasion.", "Fey Wanderer|Fey Wanderer Spells": "Once you reach the Ranger level shown, you always have that spell prepared: Ranger level 3, Charm Person; Ranger level 5, Misty Step; Ranger level 9, Summon Fey; Ranger level 13, Dimension Door; Ranger level 17, Mislead. **Feywild Gifts.** You also carry a fey blessing. Pick it from this list or roll 1d6 to decide: (1) during any Short or Long Rest you take, illusory butterflies flutter about you; (2) each dawn, flowers bloom in your hair; (3) you give off a faint smell of cinnamon, lavender, nutmeg, or some other comforting herb or spice; (4) your shadow dances whenever nobody is looking straight at it; (5) horns or antlers grow from your head; (6) the color of your skin and hair shifts every dawn.", "Fey Wanderer|Beguiling Twist": "Feywild magic shields your mind, granting you Advantage on any saving throw against the Charmed or Frightened condition, whether the roll is to avoid the condition or to end it. In addition, whenever such a saving throw succeeds for you or for a creature within 120 feet of you that you can see, you can take a Reaction to turn the magic on another creature within 120 feet of you that you can see. That creature makes a Wisdom saving throw, using your spell save DC. If it fails, you choose whether it becomes Charmed or Frightened, and that condition lasts 1 minute. It tries the saving throw again each time one of its turns ends, freeing itself from the effect on a success.", "Fey Wanderer|Fey Reinforcements": "You can cast Summon Fey with no Material component. You can also cast it once without spending a spell slot, and you regain that slot-free casting when you finish a Long Rest. Each time you start casting the spell, you can change it so that it doesn't need Concentration. If you do, the spell lasts 1 minute for that casting.", "Fey Wanderer|Misty Wanderer": "You can cast Misty Step without spending a spell slot. The number of times you can do so equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and every expended use comes back when you finish a Long Rest. In addition, each time you cast Misty Step, you can take one willing creature along, provided it is within 5 feet of you and you can see it. It teleports as well, arriving in an unoccupied space you choose that lies no more than 5 feet from the space where you arrive.", "Gloom Stalker|Dread Ambusher": "**Ambusher's Leap.** When your first turn of each combat begins, your Speed is 10 feet higher until that turn ends. **Dreadful Strike.** If you hit a creature with a weapon attack, you can have the attack deal an extra 2d6 Psychic damage. This benefit works no more than once per turn. The number of uses equals your Wisdom modifier (minimum of once), and finishing a Long Rest restores every spent use. **Initiative Bonus.** You can add your Wisdom modifier to each Initiative roll you make.", "Gloom Stalker|Gloom Stalker Spells": "You always have each of these spells prepared once you reach the Ranger level given for it: Disguise Self at level 3, Rope Trick at level 5, Fear at level 9, Greater Invisibility at level 13, and Seeming at level 17.", "Gloom Stalker|Umbral Sight": "You gain Darkvision out to 60 feet. If you already had Darkvision when you got this feature, its range grows by 60 feet instead. You are also skilled at evading creatures that depend on Darkvision. While you are entirely in Darkness, you have the Invisible condition against any creature that depends on Darkvision to see you there.", "Gloom Stalker|Iron Mind": "You become proficient in Wisdom saving throws. If you already have that proficiency, you instead become proficient in your choice of Intelligence or Charisma saving throws.", "Gloom Stalker|Stalker's Flurry": "Your Dreadful Strike's Psychic damage increases to 2d8. Also, whenever you use the Dreadful Strike benefit of your Dread Ambusher feature, you can add one of these effects. **Sudden Strike.** You can attack again with the same weapon, targeting a different creature within 5 feet of the original target, provided that creature is also within the weapon's range. **Mass Fear.** Every creature within 10 feet of the target, as well as the target itself, must attempt a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. Each creature that fails has the Frightened condition until your next turn starts.", "Gloom Stalker|Shadowy Dodge": "When an attack roll is made against you, you can respond with a Reaction that gives the roll Disadvantage. Then, whether the attack hits or misses, you can teleport up to 30 feet, arriving in an unoccupied space you can see.", "Hunter|Hunter's Lore": "Nature reveals your prey's strengths and weaknesses to you. For as long as your Hunter's Mark is on a creature, you know whether it has any Immunities, Resistances, or Vulnerabilities and, if so, what each one is.", "Hunter|Hunter's Prey": "Choose one of the following options. Each time you finish a Short or Long Rest, you can swap the option you chose for the other one. **Colossus Slayer.** If you hit a creature with a weapon while that creature is missing any of its Hit Points, the weapon deals an extra 1d8 damage to it. This extra damage can happen only once per turn. **Horde Breaker.** Once during each of your turns, when you attack with a weapon, you can make one more attack with that same weapon. This extra attack must target a different creature that you haven't attacked this turn, that is no more than 5 feet away from the first target, and that is inside the weapon's range.", "Hunter|Defensive Tactics": "Choose one of the following options. Each time you finish a Short or Long Rest, you can swap the option you chose for the other one. **Escape the Horde.** Opportunity Attacks made against you have Disadvantage. **Multiattack Defense.** After a creature hits you with an attack roll, every other attack roll it makes against you this turn has Disadvantage.", "Hunter|Superior Hunter's Prey": "Once per turn, when you damage the creature marked by your Hunter's Mark, that spell's extra damage can also hit a second creature you can see that is within 30 feet of the first.", "Hunter|Superior Hunter's Defense": "Whenever you take damage, your Reaction can give you Resistance to that damage. Until the end of the current turn, that Resistance also covers further damage of that type.", "Arcane Trickster|Spellcasting": "**Cantrips.** You know three cantrips: Mage Hand and two more of your choice taken from the Wizard spell list (suggested picks are Mind Sliver and Minor Illusion). On gaining a Rogue level, you may trade one of these cantrips, except Mage Hand, for another Wizard cantrip you choose. Reaching Rogue level 10 teaches you one additional Wizard cantrip of your choice. **Spell Slots.** Your number of spell slots for level 1+ spells appears in the Arcane Trickster Spellcasting table. All expended slots come back after a Long Rest. **Prepared Spells of Level 1+.** You choose which level 1+ spells are ready for casting with this feature. Start by choosing three level 1 Wizard spells (suggested: Charm Person, Disguise Self, and Fog Cloud). As your Rogue level rises, this list grows, as shown in the Arcane Trickster Spellcasting table under Prepared Spells. Each time that number increases, add Wizard spells of your choice until the size of your list equals the number in the table. Each chosen spell must be of a level you have spell slots for. A level 7 Rogue, for instance, can have five Wizard spells prepared, any mix of level 1 and level 2 spells. **Changing Your Prepared Spells.** On gaining a Rogue level, you may replace one spell on the list with another Wizard spell of a level you have spell slots for. **Spellcasting Ability.** Intelligence is the spellcasting ability of your Wizard spells. **Spellcasting Focus.** An Arcane Focus can serve as your Spellcasting Focus for Wizard spells.", "Arcane Trickster|Mage Hand Legerdemain": "Whenever you cast Mage Hand, you can make the spectral hand Invisible, and you can cast the spell as a Bonus Action. You can control the hand with a Bonus Action, and you can use it to make Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) checks.", "Arcane Trickster|Magical Ambush": "If you cast a spell on a creature while you have the Invisible condition, the creature has Disadvantage on any saving throw against that spell that it makes during the same turn.", "Arcane Trickster|Versatile Trickster": "Your Mage Hand can distract targets. Whenever you use your Cunning Strike's Trip option on a creature, you can also apply that option to another creature within 5 feet of the spectral hand.", "Arcane Trickster|Spell Thief": "You can magically steal another spellcaster's knowledge of how to cast a spell. When a creature casts a spell whose targets include you, or whose area of effect includes you, you can take a Reaction immediately afterward to force that creature to make an Intelligence saving throw against your spell save DC. If it fails, you negate the spell's effect on you, and if the spell is level 1 or higher and of a level you can cast, you also steal the knowledge of it, whether or not it is a Wizard spell. You have the stolen spell prepared for the next 8 hours, and the caster is unable to cast it until those 8 hours have passed. Once you have stolen a spell this way, this feature is unavailable to you until you finish a Long Rest.", "Assassin|Assassinate": "**Initiative.** Your Initiative rolls have Advantage. **Surprising Strikes.** In the first round of every combat, your attack rolls have Advantage against any creature that hasn't yet taken a turn. If your Sneak Attack hits a target during that round, the target also takes extra damage equal to your Rogue level, of the same type as the weapon's damage.", "Assassin|Assassin's Tools": "You obtain a Poisoner's Kit and a Disguise Kit, and you become proficient with both.", "Assassin|Infiltration Expertise": "**Masterful Mimicry.** After spending at least 1 hour studying another person, you can unerringly copy that person's speech, handwriting, or both. **Roving Aim.** Using Steady Aim doesn't reduce your Speed to 0.", "Assassin|Envenom Weapons": "Whenever a target fails the saving throw against the Poison option of your Cunning Strike, it also takes 2d6 Poison damage. Resistance to Poison damage doesn't apply to this damage.", "Assassin|Death Strike": "When your Sneak Attack hits a target in the first round of a combat, that target makes a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 + your Dexterity modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. If the target fails, the attack's damage against it is doubled.", "Soulknife|Psionic Power": "A wellspring of psionic energy lies within you. Your Psionic Energy Dice represent it and power certain abilities of this subclass. The Soulknife Energy Dice table sets the number and size of these dice by Rogue level: four d6s at level 3, six d8s at level 5, eight d8s at level 9, eight d10s at level 11, ten d10s at level 13, and twelve d12s at level 17. Any feature of this subclass that uses a Psionic Energy Die uses only these dice. Some powers expend a Psionic Energy Die, as their descriptions state, and you can't use a power that requires a die while all your dice are expended. Finishing a Short Rest restores one expended die, and finishing a Long Rest restores all of them. **Psi-Bolstered Knack.** When an ability check using a skill or tool you're proficient with fails, you can add the roll of one Psionic Energy Die to the check, which might turn the failure into a success. The die counts as expended only if the check then succeeds. **Psychic Whispers.** You can open telepathic links between yourself and others. Take a Magic action to pick one or more creatures you can see, no more than your Proficiency Bonus in number, and roll one Psionic Energy Die. The chosen creatures and you can then talk to one another telepathically. The connection lasts a number of hours equal to the number you rolled. Sending or receiving a message requires no action, but it works only while you and the other creature are no more than 1 mile apart. Any participant may break off the telepathic link whenever it likes, which requires no action. Your first use of this power after each Long Rest costs no die. Any other use expends the die.", "Soulknife|Psychic Blades": "You can create shimmering blades of psychic energy. When you make an Opportunity Attack or take the Attack action, you can form a Psychic Blade in your free hand and use it for the attack. The magic blade has these traits: it is a Simple Melee weapon; on a hit it deals 1d6 Psychic damage plus the ability modifier you used for the attack roll; it has the Finesse and Thrown (range 60/120 feet) properties; and its mastery property is Vex, which you can use without it counting toward your Weapon Mastery limit on properties. The blade disappears the moment it hits or misses, and if it deals damage, it leaves no mark. Once you have attacked with the blade on your turn, you can take a Bonus Action that turn to attack with a second psychic blade, either in melee or at range, if your other hand is free to form it. This bonus attack uses a 1d4 damage die instead of a 1d6.", "Soulknife|Soul Blades": "Your Psychic Blades gain the following powers. **Homing Strikes.** When an attack roll you make with your Psychic Blade misses the target, you can add the roll of one Psionic Energy Die to that attack roll. If the attack then hits, the die is expended. **Psychic Teleportation.** You can take a Bonus Action to form a Psychic Blade, expend a Psionic Energy Die, and roll it. You then hurl the blade toward an unoccupied space you can see whose distance from you is at most 10 feet times the number rolled, and you teleport into that space as the blade disappears.", "Soulknife|Psychic Veil": "You can mask yourself with a veil of psychic static. As a Magic action, you can turn yourself Invisible. The veil lasts 1 hour, and you can dismiss it at any time (no action required). The invisibility ends early the moment you damage a creature or make a creature attempt a saving throw. After using this feature, you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest, or earlier by expending one Psionic Energy Die (no action required).", "Soulknife|Rend Mind": "When you deal Sneak Attack damage to a creature with your Psychic Blades, you can make that target attempt a Wisdom saving throw. The DC equals 8 + your Dexterity modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. If it fails, it has the Stunned condition for 1 minute. The Stunned creature repeats the save whenever one of its turns ends, and the effect on it ends if it succeeds. After using this feature, you regain the use when you finish a Long Rest, or earlier by expending three Psionic Energy Dice (no action required).", "Thief|Fast Hands": "With a Bonus Action, you can perform either of these options. **Sleight of Hand.** You make a Dexterity (Sleight of Hand) check, either to pick a pocket or to pick a lock or disarm a trap using Thieves' Tools. **Use an Object.** You take the Utilize action, or you use a magic item that requires the Magic action by taking that action.", "Thief|Second-Story Work": "You have trained to reach places that are especially hard to get to. **Climber.** You have a Climb Speed that equals your Speed. **Jumper.** Your jump distance can be determined by your Dexterity instead of your Strength.", "Thief|Supreme Sneak": "Your Cunning Strike gains a new option. **Stealth Attack (Cost: 1d6).** While you have the Invisible condition from the Hide action, this attack doesn't end it, as long as you finish the turn behind Three-Quarters Cover or Total Cover.", "Thief|Use Magic Device": "**Attunement.** You can attune to as many as four magic items at the same time. **Charges.** Whenever a magic item property you use would expend charges, roll 1d6. If you roll a 6, the property works and the charges aren't expended. **Scrolls.** Any Spell Scroll is usable by you, and Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for its spell. A cantrip or level 1 spell on a scroll can be cast reliably. For a higher-level spell, you must first pass an Intelligence (Arcana) check (DC equal to 10 + the spell's level). If you pass, you cast the spell from the scroll. If you fail, the scroll disintegrates.", "Thief|Thief's Reflexes": "You are skilled at setting ambushes and slipping away from danger. During the first round of any combat, you can take two turns: the first at your normal Initiative and the second at your Initiative minus 10.", "Aberrant Sorcery|Psionic Spells": "Starting at the Sorcerer level in parentheses, each of these is always prepared for you: Mind Sliver, Dissonant Whispers, Detect Thoughts, Calm Emotions, Arms of Hadar (3); Sending, Hunger of Hadar (5); Summon Aberration, Evard's Black Tentacles (7); Telekinesis, Rary's Telepathic Bond (9).", "Aberrant Sorcery|Telepathic Speech": "You can link your mind telepathically to another creature's mind. As a Bonus Action, pick one creature within 30 feet of you that you can see. You and that creature can then communicate telepathically as long as the distance between you is no more than a number of miles equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 mile). For the two of you to understand each other, each of you must mentally use a language the other one knows. The link ends after a number of minutes equal to your Sorcerer level, or sooner if you use this ability to form a link with a different creature.", "Aberrant Sorcery|Psionic Sorcery": "Whenever you cast a level 1+ spell granted by your Psionic Spells feature, you can pay for it either with a spell slot as usual or by spending as many Sorcery Points as the spell's level. A spell cast with Sorcery Points needs no Verbal or Somatic components, and it needs no Material components unless the spell consumes them or names a cost for them.", "Aberrant Sorcery|Psychic Defenses": "You gain Resistance to Psychic damage. In addition, saving throws you make to avoid the Charmed or Frightened condition, or to end either one, have Advantage.", "Aberrant Sorcery|Revelation in Flesh": "You can release the aberrant truth hidden inside you. As a Bonus Action, you can spend 1 or more Sorcery Points to magically transform your body for 10 minutes. Each Sorcery Point you spend grants you one benefit of your choice from the options below, and each chosen benefit lasts until the transformation ends. **Aquatic Adaptation.** You gain a Swim Speed of twice your Speed, and you can breathe underwater. Your neck sprouts gills, or gills flare behind your ears, and webbing forms between your fingers or wriggling cilia grow from you. **Glistening Flight.** Your Speed also becomes your Fly Speed, and you can hover. While you are flying, mucus or otherworldly light makes your skin glisten. **See the Invisible.** You can see every Invisible creature within 60 feet of you, unless the creature is behind Total Cover. Your eyes also change, turning black or becoming writhing sensory tendrils. **Wormlike Movement.** Your body, together with any equipment you wear or carry, turns slimy and pliable. You can move through spaces as narrow as 1 inch, and by spending 5 feet of movement you can escape nonmagical restraints or the Grappled condition.", "Aberrant Sorcery|Warping Implosion": "You can release an anomaly that warps space. As a Magic action, you teleport up to 120 feet away, arriving in an unoccupied space you can see. The moment you vanish, each creature no more than 30 feet from the space you left makes a Strength saving throw against your spell save DC. A creature that fails takes 3d10 Force damage and gets pulled in a straight line toward your former space, ending in the unoccupied space nearest to that former space. A creature that succeeds takes only half as much damage. After you use this feature, it becomes available again when you finish a Long Rest, or sooner if you spend 5 Sorcery Points to regain it (no action required).", "Clockwork Sorcery|Clockwork Spells": "Starting at the Sorcerer level in parentheses, each of these is always prepared for you: Protection from Evil and Good, Lesser Restoration, Alarm, Aid (3); Protection from Energy, Dispel Magic (5); Summon Construct, Freedom of Movement (7); Wall of Force, Greater Restoration (9). **Manifestations of Order.** You also choose, or roll 1d6 to decide, how your bond with order shows itself while you cast any of your Sorcerer spells: (1) ghostly cogwheels float behind you; (2) clock hands spin within your eyes; (3) your skin shines with a brassy glow; (4) floating equations and geometric objects cover your body; (5) your Spellcasting Focus briefly turns into a Tiny clockwork mechanism; (6) you and the creatures your magic affects can hear gears ticking or a clock chiming.", "Clockwork Sorcery|Restore Balance": "Your link to the plane of absolute order lets you even out chaotic moments. If a creature within 60 feet of you that you can see is going to roll a d20 that has Advantage or Disadvantage, you can take a Reaction so that neither Advantage nor Disadvantage affects that roll. The number of times you can use this feature equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and finishing a Long Rest restores every expended use.", "Clockwork Sorcery|Bastion of Law": "By tapping into the grand equation of existence, you can surround a creature with a shimmering shield of order. You can take a Magic action and spend 1 to 5 Sorcery Points, placing a magical ward around yourself or around another creature within 30 feet of you that you can see. The ward consists of a number of d8s equal to the Sorcery Points you spent to create it. Whenever the warded creature takes damage, it can expend any number of those dice, roll them, and lower the damage it takes by the total. The ward remains until you use this feature again or finish a Long Rest.", "Clockwork Sorcery|Trance of Order": "Your consciousness can sync with the endless calculations of Mechanus. You can take a Bonus Action to enter this state, which lasts 1 minute. During that time, attack rolls made against you can't benefit from Advantage, and each time you make a D20 Test, you can count a d20 result of 9 or lower as a 10. After you use this feature, it becomes available again when you finish a Long Rest, or sooner if you spend 5 Sorcery Points to regain it (no action required).", "Clockwork Sorcery|Clockwork Cavalcade": "You briefly call up spirits of order to wipe away the disorder around you. As a Magic action, you call the spirits into a 30-foot Cube originating from you. The spirits take the form of modrons or other Constructs, as you choose. Being intangible and invulnerable, they create the effects below within the Cube and then vanish. After you use this action, it becomes available again when you finish a Long Rest, or sooner if you spend 7 Sorcery Points to regain it (no action required). **Heal.** Up to 100 Hit Points are restored by the spirits, divided however you like among any number of creatures you choose in the Cube. **Repair.** Every damaged object entirely inside the Cube is instantly repaired. **Dispel.** Each spell of level 6 or lower ends on the creatures and objects of your choice in the Cube.", "Draconic Sorcery|Draconic Resilience": "Your draconic gift shows itself in your body. Your Hit Point maximum goes up by 3, and it goes up by 1 more each time you gain another Sorcerer level. Dragon-like scales also cover parts of you. While you wear no armor, your base Armor Class equals 10 + your Dexterity modifier + your Charisma modifier.", "Draconic Sorcery|Draconic Spells": "Starting at the Sorcerer level in parentheses, each of these is always prepared for you: Dragon's Breath, Command, Chromatic Orb, Alter Self (3); Fly, Fear (5); Charm Monster, Arcane Eye (7); Summon Dragon, Legend Lore (9).", "Draconic Sorcery|Elemental Affinity": "Your draconic magic is attuned to one damage type linked to dragons. Pick Acid, Cold, Fire, Lightning, or Poison as that type. You gain Resistance to it. Also, each time a spell you cast deals damage of that type, one of the spell's damage rolls can include your Charisma modifier as a bonus.", "Draconic Sorcery|Dragon Wings": "As a Bonus Action, you can make draconic wings appear on your back. They stay for 1 hour, though you can dismiss them sooner (no action required), and while they last, you have a Fly Speed of 60 feet. After you use this feature, it becomes available again when you finish a Long Rest, or sooner if you spend 3 Sorcery Points to regain it (no action required).", "Draconic Sorcery|Dragon Companion": "You can cast Summon Dragon with no Material component. You can also cast it once without spending a spell slot, and you regain that slot-free casting when you finish a Long Rest. Each time you start casting the spell, you can change it so that it doesn't need Concentration. If you do, the spell lasts 1 minute for that casting.", "Wild Magic Sorcery|Wild Magic Surge": "Bursts of untamed magic can erupt from your spellcasting. Once per turn, right after you cast a Sorcerer spell using a spell slot, you can roll 1d20. On a 20, you roll on the Wild Magic Surge table to produce a magical effect. If the resulting effect is a spell, it is too wild for your Metamagic to affect it. **Wild Magic Surge Table.** Roll 1d100 and apply the matching result. 01-04: For the next minute, you roll on this table once more when each of your turns starts; if this result comes up again in that time, ignore it. 05-08: A creature Friendly toward you shows up in an unoccupied space within 60 feet of you, chosen at random. The Dungeon Master controls it, and it disappears after 1 minute. Roll 1d4 for the creature: 1, a Modron Duodrone; 2, a Flumph; 3, a Modron Monodrone; 4, a Unicorn. Its stat block is in the Monster Manual. 09-12: You regain 5 Hit Points when each of your turns starts, for the next minute. 13-16: If, within the next minute, you cast a spell that involves a saving throw, creatures have Disadvantage on their saving throws against the first such spell. 17-20: An effect is imposed on you for 1 minute, unless its description gives a different duration. Roll 1d8 for the effect: 1, faint ethereal music surrounds you, audible only to you and to creatures within 5 feet of you; 2, you grow by one size category; 3, a long beard of feathers grows on you and stays until you sneeze, when the feathers burst from your face and vanish; 4, you have to shout whenever you speak; 5, illusory butterflies flit through the air within 10 feet of you; 6, an eye appears on your forehead, giving you Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks; 7, pink bubbles drift out of your mouth each time you speak; 8, your skin takes on a vibrant blue hue for 24 hours or until a Remove Curse spell ends the effect. 21-24: For the next minute, any spell of yours that normally takes an action to cast takes a Bonus Action instead. 25-28: You are sent to the Astral Plane until your next turn ends. Then you come back to the space you left, or to the nearest unoccupied space if that one is occupied. 29-32: Within the next minute, the next damage-dealing spell you cast uses the maximum value of every damage die instead of rolling those dice. 33-36: For the next minute, you have Resistance to all damage. 37-40: You become a potted plant until your next turn starts. As a plant, you have the Incapacitated condition and Vulnerability to all damage. Your pot breaks and your form reverts if your Hit Points drop to 0. 41-44: For the next minute, you can take a Bonus Action on each of your turns to teleport up to 20 feet. 45-48: Pick up to three creatures within 30 feet of you. They and you have the Invisible condition for 1 minute. The invisibility on a creature ends right after that creature casts a spell, deals damage, or makes an attack roll. 49-52: For the next minute, a spectral shield hovers near you, giving you a +2 bonus to Armor Class and immunity to Magic Missile. 53-56: On this turn, you can take one extra action. 57-60: You cast a random spell. If it normally needs Concentration, this casting doesn't, and the spell lasts for its full duration. Roll 1d10 for the spell: 1, Confusion; 2, Fireball; 3, Fog Cloud; 4, Fly, targeting a random creature within 60 feet of you; 5, Grease; 6, Levitate, targeting yourself; 7, Magic Missile, as a level 5 spell; 8, Mirror Image; 9, Polymorph, targeting yourself, and a failed saving throw turns you into a Goat (its stat block is in appendix B); 10, See Invisibility. 61-64: For the next minute, whenever you touch a flammable, nonmagical object that no other creature is wearing or carrying, the object catches fire: it takes 1d4 Fire damage and is burning. 65-68: Should you die within the next hour, you come back to life at once, as the Reincarnate spell would revive you. 69-72: Until your next turn ends, you have the Frightened condition. The Dungeon Master decides what you are afraid of. 73-76: You teleport to an unoccupied space up to 60 feet away that you can see. 77-80: One creature within 60 feet of you, chosen at random, has the Poisoned condition for 1d4 hours. 81-84: For the next minute, you shed Bright Light in a 30-foot radius. Each creature that finishes its turn no more than 5 feet from you has the Blinded condition until its next turn ends. 85-88: Pick up to three creatures you can see no more than 30 feet away from you. Each of them takes 1d10 Necrotic damage. You then regain as many Hit Points as the total Necrotic damage dealt this way. 89-92: Pick up to three creatures you can see no more than 30 feet away from you. Each takes 4d10 Lightning damage. 93-96: For the next minute, Vulnerability to Piercing damage applies to you and to all creatures within 30 feet of you. 97-00: Roll 1d6: 1, you regain 2d10 Hit Points; 2, you pick one ally within 300 feet of you, and it regains 2d10 Hit Points; 3, your lowest-level expended spell slot is restored to you; 4, an ally you choose within 300 feet of you regains its lowest-level expended spell slot; 5, you regain all your expended Sorcery Points; 6, every effect listed for row 17-20 affects you at the same time.", "Wild Magic Sorcery|Tides of Chaos": "You can bend chaos itself to gain Advantage on a single D20 Test, choosing to do so before you roll the d20. After you do so, you can't use this feature again until you either cast a Sorcerer spell using a spell slot or finish a Long Rest. If, after using it, you cast a Sorcerer spell with a spell slot before finishing a Long Rest, that casting automatically makes you roll on the Wild Magic Surge table.", "Wild Magic Sorcery|Bend Luck": "You can twist fate with your wild magic. When another creature you can see makes a D20 Test, you can respond right after its d20 roll by taking a Reaction and spending 1 Sorcery Point. Roll 1d4 and apply the number rolled to that d20 roll as a bonus or a penalty (your choice).", "Wild Magic Sorcery|Controlled Chaos": "You gain a measure of control over your wild magic surges. When a roll on the Wild Magic Surge table is called for, you can roll twice and keep either number.", "Wild Magic Sorcery|Tamed Surge": "Right after you cast a Sorcerer spell using a spell slot, you can pick an effect from the Wild Magic Surge table and create it, rather than rolling on the table. Any effect except the one in the table's final row is allowed, and if the effect you pick calls for a roll, you must make that roll. Once used, this feature is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest.", "Archfey Patron|Archfey Spells": "Starting at the Warlock level in parentheses, each of these is always prepared for you: Sleep, Phantasmal Force, Misty Step, Faerie Fire, Calm Emotions (3); Plant Growth, Blink (5); Greater Invisibility, Dominate Beast (7); Seeming, Dominate Person (9).", "Archfey Patron|Steps of the Fey": "Your patron grants you passage across the boundaries of the planes. Misty Step is yours to cast without a spell slot, and the number of such castings equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of once). All expended castings return when you finish a Long Rest. Whenever you cast the spell, you can add one of the following effects. **Refreshing Step.** As soon as the teleport ends, you or a creature within 10 feet of you that you can see gains 1d10 Temporary Hit Points. **Taunting Step.** Every creature within 5 feet of your starting space makes a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. A creature that fails has Disadvantage, until the start of your next turn, on any attack roll that targets someone other than you.", "Archfey Patron|Misty Escape": "When you take damage, you can respond by casting Misty Step as a Reaction. You also add two new effects to the options of your Steps of the Fey feature. **Disappearing Step.** You gain the Invisible condition, which lasts until your next turn starts but ends early right after you deal damage, make an attack roll, or cast a spell. **Dreadful Step.** Choose either the space you teleported out of or the space you arrive in. Each creature within 5 feet of that space makes a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC and takes 2d10 Psychic damage if it fails.", "Archfey Patron|Beguiling Defenses": "Your patron has taught you to protect your mind and body. You have Immunity to the Charmed condition. Also, right after an attack roll from a creature you can see hits you, you can take a Reaction to cut the damage you take in half (round down). With that Reaction, you can also make the attacker attempt a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. If it fails, it takes Psychic damage equal to the damage you take. After you use this Reaction, it becomes available again when you finish a Long Rest, or sooner if you expend a Pact Magic spell slot to regain it (no action required).", "Archfey Patron|Bewitching Magic": "Your patron lets you weave teleportation into your magic. Whenever you use an action and a spell slot to cast an Illusion or Enchantment spell, you can cast Misty Step right afterward as part of that action, and this casting doesn't expend a spell slot.", "Celestial Patron|Celestial Spells": "Starting at the Warlock level in parentheses, each of these is always prepared for you: Sacred Flame, Light, Lesser Restoration, Guiding Bolt, Cure Wounds, Aid (3); Revivify, Daylight (5); Wall of Fire, Guardian of Faith (7); Summon Celestial, Greater Restoration (9).", "Celestial Patron|Healing Light": "Celestial energy flows through you to mend wounds. This healing is fueled by a pool of d6s, which holds a number of dice equal to 1 plus your Warlock level. You can take a Bonus Action to heal yourself or one creature within 60 feet of you that you can see, expending dice from the pool. You can expend no more dice at once than your Charisma modifier (minimum of one die). Roll those dice, and the target regains Hit Points equal to their total. Finishing a Long Rest refills the pool with all its expended dice.", "Celestial Patron|Radiant Soul": "Your bond with your patron lets radiant energy flow through you. You have Resistance to Radiant damage. In addition, once per turn, when one of your spells deals Radiant or Fire damage, you can choose one of the spell's targets and add your Charisma modifier to the damage the spell deals to it.", "Celestial Patron|Celestial Resilience": "Each time you finish a Short or Long Rest or use your Magical Cunning feature, you receive Temporary Hit Points in an amount equal to your Warlock level plus your Charisma modifier. When you receive them, you can also pick up to five creatures you can see. Each of those creatures gains Temporary Hit Points too, in an amount equal to your Charisma modifier plus half your Warlock level.", "Celestial Patron|Searing Vengeance": "When a Death Saving Throw is about to be rolled by you or by an ally within 60 feet of you, you can release radiant energy to rescue that creature. The creature regains Hit Points totaling half its Hit Point maximum, and it can end the Prone condition on itself. Then every creature you choose within 30 feet of the rescued creature takes 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier in Radiant damage and has the Blinded condition until the current turn ends. After you use this feature, it is unavailable until you finish a Long Rest.", "Fiend Patron|Dark One's Blessing": "Each time an enemy drops to 0 Hit Points because of you, you gain Temporary Hit Points in an amount equal to your Charisma modifier plus your Warlock level, with a minimum of 1. The same benefit applies when someone else reduces to 0 Hit Points an enemy that is within 10 feet of you.", "Fiend Patron|Fiend Spells": "Starting at the Warlock level in parentheses, each of these is always prepared for you: Suggestion, Scorching Ray, Command, Burning Hands (3); Stinking Cloud, Fireball (5); Wall of Fire, Fire Shield (7); Insect Plague, Geas (9).", "Fiend Patron|Dark One's Own Luck": "Your fiendish patron lets you bend fate in your favor. When you roll for an ability check or saving throw, this feature lets you add a d10 to the total. You may decide after seeing the roll, as long as none of the roll's effects have happened yet. The number of times you can use this feature equals your Charisma modifier (minimum of once), and you can't use it more than once on the same roll. All expended uses return when you finish a Long Rest.", "Fiend Patron|Fiendish Resilience": "Each time you finish a Short or Long Rest, pick one damage type other than Force. You have Resistance to the chosen type until you pick a different one with this feature.", "Fiend Patron|Hurl Through Hell": "Once per turn, when an attack roll of yours hits a creature, you can attempt to send that target on an instant trip through the Lower Planes. The target makes a Charisma saving throw against your spell save DC. On a failure, it vanishes and tumbles through a nightmarish landscape. Unless it is a Fiend, it takes 8d10 Psychic damage. It is also Incapacitated until your next turn ends, and at that point it comes back to the space it occupied before or to the nearest unoccupied space. After you use this feature, it recharges when you finish a Long Rest. You can also restore its use by expending a Pact Magic spell slot, which requires no action.", "Great Old One Patron|Awakened Mind": "You can link your mind telepathically with the mind of someone else. As a Bonus Action, pick one creature within 30 feet of you that you can see. You and that creature can then communicate with each other telepathically as long as you are no more than a certain number of miles apart, equal to your Charisma modifier (minimum of 1 mile). The two of you understand each other only if each of you mentally uses a language the other knows. The link lasts for minutes equal to your Warlock level. Using this feature to connect with a different creature ends the earlier link.", "Great Old One Patron|Great Old One Spells": "Your patron's magic keeps certain spells always ready for you. Once you reach a Warlock level shown below, you always have the spells listed for that level prepared from then on. Warlock level 3: Detect Thoughts, Dissonant Whispers, Phantasmal Force, and Tasha's Hideous Laughter. Warlock level 5: Clairvoyance and Hunger of Hadar. Warlock level 7: Confusion and Summon Aberration. Warlock level 9: Modify Memory and Telekinesis.", "Great Old One Patron|Psychic Spells": "Whenever a Warlock spell you cast deals damage, you can make its damage type Psychic instead. You can also cast any Warlock spell of the Enchantment or Illusion school without providing its Verbal or Somatic components.", "Great Old One Patron|Clairvoyant Combatant": "Whenever Awakened Mind creates a telepathic bond between you and a creature, you can have that creature attempt a Wisdom saving throw against your spell save DC. If it fails, then for as long as the bond lasts, its attack rolls against you are made with Disadvantage, while you make attack rolls against it with Advantage. Once you use this feature, its use returns when you finish a Short or Long Rest. You may also restore it early by expending a Pact Magic spell slot, which requires no action.", "Great Old One Patron|Eldritch Hex": "Your otherworldly patron bestows a potent curse on you. Hex is always among your prepared spells. Whenever you cast it and pick an ability, the target also suffers Disadvantage on saving throws that use that ability until the spell ends.", "Great Old One Patron|Thought Shield": "Neither telepathy nor any other method can read your thoughts unless you permit it. Psychic damage is something you have Resistance to, and any creature that deals Psychic damage to you takes damage equal to the amount you took.", "Great Old One Patron|Create Thrall": "When you cast Summon Aberration, you can alter the spell so that it doesn't need Concentration. If you do, that casting's duration becomes 1 minute, and the Aberration appears with a number of Temporary Hit Points that equals your Charisma modifier plus your Warlock level. Also, the first time on each turn that the Aberration hits a creature affected by your Hex, it deals extra Psychic damage to that target equal to the spell's bonus damage.", "Abjurer|Abjuration Savant": "Pick two Wizard spells of the Abjuration school, each of level 2 or lower, and add them to your spellbook at no cost. Also, each time this class gives you access to spell slots of a new level, you can add one more Wizard spell of the Abjuration school to your spellbook at no cost, and its level must be one you have spell slots for.", "Abjurer|Arcane Ward": "You can wrap yourself in protective magic. When you cast an Abjuration spell using a spell slot, you can at the same moment draw on a strand of that spell's magic to form a magical ward around yourself. The ward lasts until you finish a Long Rest, and its Hit Point maximum equals twice your Wizard level plus your Intelligence modifier. Any damage you take hits the ward instead of you. Apply any Resistances or Vulnerabilities you have before the ward loses Hit Points. If the damage drops the ward to 0 Hit Points, any damage left over is dealt to you. While at 0 Hit Points, the ward can't absorb damage, but its magic persists. Each time you cast an Abjuration spell using a spell slot, the ward regains Hit Points equal to twice the slot's level. As an alternative, you can take a Bonus Action to expend a spell slot, and the ward regains Hit Points equal to twice the level of the expended slot. Creating the ward again requires you to finish a Long Rest first.", "Abjurer|Projected Ward": "When a creature takes damage while it is within 30 feet of you and you can see it, you can use a Reaction to have your Arcane Ward absorb that damage. If the ward drops to 0 Hit Points from it, the protected creature takes whatever damage remains. Apply that creature's Resistances or Vulnerabilities, if any, before the ward loses Hit Points.", "Abjurer|Spell Breaker": "Counterspell and Dispel Magic are always prepared for you. You may cast Dispel Magic with a Bonus Action, and you may also add your Proficiency Bonus to that spell's ability check. When you cast either of these spells using a spell slot and the spell fails to stop a spell, the slot isn't expended.", "Abjurer|Spell Resistance": "You have Resistance to damage from spells, and your saving throws against spells are made with Advantage.", "Diviner|Divination Savant": "Pick two Wizard spells of the Divination school, each of level 2 or lower, and add them to your spellbook at no cost. Also, each time this class gives you access to spell slots of a new level, you can add one more Wizard spell of the Divination school to your spellbook at no cost, and its level must be one you have spell slots for.", "Diviner|Portent": "Flashes of the future start to crowd into your awareness. Each time you finish a Long Rest, roll two d20s and write down the results. You can swap one of these foretelling rolls in for any D20 Test made by you or by a creature you can see. You must decide to do this before the roll happens, and you can make such a swap only once per turn. Every foretelling roll is good for a single use, and you lose any unused ones when you finish a Long Rest.", "Diviner|Expert Divination": "Divination magic comes so naturally to you that casting it uses up only part of your spellcasting effort. Whenever you cast a Divination spell with a spell slot of level 2 or higher, you regain one expended spell slot. The regained slot must be lower in level than the slot you used, and it can't be above level 5.", "Diviner|The Third Eye": "You can sharpen your powers of perception. As a Bonus Action, pick one of the benefits below. It lasts until you start a Short or Long Rest. After you use this feature, you must finish a Short or Long Rest to use it again. **Darkvision.** You gain Darkvision out to 120 feet. **Greater Comprehension.** You are able to read all languages. **See Invisibility.** You can cast See Invisibility, and doing so doesn't expend a spell slot.", "Diviner|Greater Portent": "Your dream visions grow stronger, showing you a clearer picture of what lies ahead. You roll three d20s for your Portent feature instead of two.", "Evoker|Evocation Savant": "Pick two Wizard spells of the Evocation school, each of level 2 or lower, and add them to your spellbook at no cost. Also, each time this class gives you access to spell slots of a new level, you can add one more Wizard spell of the Evocation school to your spellbook at no cost, and its level must be one you have spell slots for.", "Evoker|Potent Cantrip": "Even creatures that dodge the worst of your damaging cantrips still feel them. When you cast a cantrip at a creature and either your attack roll misses or the target succeeds on its saving throw against the cantrip, the target still takes half the cantrip's damage (if it deals any), but it suffers none of the cantrip's other effects.", "Evoker|Sculpt Spells": "You can carve out pockets of relative safety inside your evocations. Whenever an Evocation spell you cast affects other creatures you can see, you can choose a number of those creatures equal to 1 plus the spell's level. Those you choose automatically pass their saving throws against the spell, and any of them that would normally take half damage on a successful save take no damage instead.", "Evoker|Empowered Evocation": "When you cast a Wizard spell that belongs to the Evocation school, you may choose one of its damage rolls and increase it by your Intelligence modifier.", "Evoker|Overchannel": "You can push your spells to greater power. When you cast a damage-dealing Wizard spell using a spell slot of level 1 through 5, you can make that spell deal maximum damage on the turn you cast it. Your first use of this feature carries no drawback. A second use before you finish a Long Rest deals 2d12 Necrotic damage to you per level of the spell slot, right after you cast the spell. This damage ignores Resistance and Immunity. Every further use before you finish a Long Rest raises the Necrotic damage per spell level by 1d12.", "Illusionist|Illusion Savant": "Pick two Wizard spells of the Illusion school, each of level 2 or lower, and add them to your spellbook at no cost. Also, each time this class gives you access to spell slots of a new level, you can add one more Wizard spell of the Illusion school to your spellbook at no cost, and its level must be one you have spell slots for.", "Illusionist|Improved Illusions": "Your Illusion spells don't require Verbal components, and any Illusion spell you cast that has a range of 10 feet or more gains 60 feet of extra range. You also learn the Minor Illusion cantrip, or, if you already know it, a different Wizard cantrip of your choice. This cantrip doesn't count against the number of cantrips you know. A single casting of Minor Illusion can create both a sound and an image, and you can cast it as a Bonus Action.", "Illusionist|Phantasmal Creatures": "Summon Beast and Summon Fey are always prepared for you. Whenever you cast one of them, you can switch its school to Illusion, which makes the summoned creature look spectral. You can cast the Illusion version of each of these spells without expending a spell slot, but doing so cuts the creature's Hit Points in half. After you cast either spell without a slot, you must finish a Long Rest before casting that spell that way again.", "Illusionist|Illusory Self": "If a creature's attack roll hits you, you can use a Reaction to place an illusory double of yourself between you and the attacker. The attack automatically misses you, and the illusion then fades. After you use this feature, it recharges when you finish a Short or Long Rest. Expending a spell slot of level 2 or higher (no action required) also restores its use.", "Illusionist|Illusory Reality": "You have learned to blend shadow magic into your illusions, giving them a kind of partial reality. When you cast an Illusion spell using a spell slot, you can pick one object in the illusion that is inanimate and nonmagical and turn that object real. You can do so as a Bonus Action on your turn while the spell is still active. The object stays real for 1 minute, and during that time it can't deal damage or impose any conditions. For example, you could create an illusory bridge across a chasm, make it real, and then walk across it."};
